From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:46:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: propagate a failed link retrain before the stream
 starts

msm_dp_ctrl_prepare_stream_on() retrains the link when asked to, or when
channel equalisation no longer holds, but ignores the result and
reports success. The stream is then enabled on a link that did not
train, the display enable path carries on as if it had, and the sink
stays dark.

Return the retrain error and tear the main link down again, so the
display enable path stops and the next modeset starts from a clean link.
Also treat a failed link status read in msm_dp_ctrl_channel_eq_ok() as
"not equalised" rather than evaluating an uninitialised buffer.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
index bffbd90ea69..684a088ec62 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -2352,7 +2352,8 @@ static bool msm_dp_ctrl_channel_eq_ok(struct msm_dp_ctrl_private *ctrl)
 	u8 link_status[DP_LINK_STATUS_SIZE];
 	int num_lanes = ctrl->link->link_params.num_lanes;
 
-	drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status(ctrl->aux, link_status);
+	if (drm_dp_dpcd_read_link_status(ctrl->aux, link_status))
+		return false;
 
 	return drm_dp_channel_eq_ok(link_status, num_lanes);
 }
@@ -2588,11 +2589,14 @@ int msm_dp_ctrl_prepare_stream_on(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl,
 	}
 
 	if (force_link_train || !msm_dp_ctrl_channel_eq_ok(ctrl))
-		msm_dp_ctrl_link_retrain(ctrl, panel);
+		ret = msm_dp_ctrl_link_retrain(ctrl, panel);
 
 	/* stop txing train pattern to end link training */
 	msm_dp_ctrl_clear_training_pattern(ctrl, panel, DP_PHY_DPRX);
 
+	if (ret)
+		msm_dp_ctrl_deinitialize_mainlink(ctrl, panel);
+
 	return ret;
 }
 
